 "narration": "The magnification of the eyepiece lens multiplied by the magnification of the objective lens. A ×10 eyepiece with a ×40 objective gives ×400. An eyepiece of ×10 and an objective of ×40 give ×400, not ×50. You can also work out the magnification of a drawing or photograph. Magnification = image size ÷ actual size, which can be rearranged to actual size = image size ÷ magnification. A student's drawing of a cheek cell is 48 mm wide, and the magnification of the drawing is ×800. 48 ÷ 800 = 0.06 mm. Convert to micrometres by multiplying by 1000: 0.06 × 1000 = 60 µm.",
 "narration_sentences": [
  "The magnification of the eyepiece lens multiplied by the magnification of the objective lens.",
  "A ×10 eyepiece with a ×40 objective gives ×400.",
  "An eyepiece of ×10 and an objective of ×40 give ×400, not ×50.",
  "You can also work out the magnification of a drawing or photograph.",
  "Magnification = image size ÷ actual size, which can be rearranged to actual size = image size ÷ magnification.",
  "A student's drawing of a cheek cell is 48 mm wide, and the magnification of the drawing is ×800.",
  "48 ÷ 800 = 0.06 mm.",
  "Convert to micrometres by multiplying by 1000: 0.06 × 1000 = 60 µm."
 ],
